  "limitations": [
    "The custom engine covers BTC only; every condition (regime, ATH, drawdown, Mayer, price vs SMA200, weekly RSI, MVRV) is derived from the archived Coin Metrics daily series.",
    "Money-weighted return (IRR) is the headline for contribution strategies; it rewards well-timed contributions and is not a buy-and-hold CAGR.",
    "Execution cost is a flat per-side basis-point assumption on every buy and sell; no slippage, spread, market impact or partial fills.",
    "Uninvested cash earns nothing. The lump-sum benchmark assumes every future contribution was available on day one — hindsight capital, shown for contrast only.",
    "Maximum drawdown is measured against a peak that steps up with each contribution, isolating market declines from contribution pace.",
    "About one BTC cycle is covered — descriptive, not walk-forward-validated or statistically significant.",
    "Acquisition remains locally supervised; an always-on host is still outstanding."
  ]
